Bootstrap Chain Milestones
==========================

Version  Milestone
-------  ---------
00       Minimal DATA-only bootstrap (129 bytes)
01       Single-character labels and strings in DATA (250 bytes)
02       First non-standard 6502 mnemonics
03       Source becomes human-readable assembly
04       Byte selectors, label assignments, origin setting
05       Two-pass assembly (forward references)
06       Hash tables for label/instruction lookup
07       Instruction table generator (instgen)
08       Error diagnostics, line numbers, stderr output
09       .include directive, file stack
10       Sections (.zeropage/.code), command-line arguments
11       Local labels, heap-based global label storage
12       Standard 6502 syntax (all 13 addressing modes), forward reference tracking
13       Source transitions to standard syntax (standard syntax migration)
14       Expression evaluation, .data directive
15       .ifdef/.endif conditional assembly
16       Macros, << >> shift operators
17       Data directives, decimal constants, memory protection
18       Self-hosting, .ifndef/.else


Source Syntax Evolution
=======================
Each version's source can only use syntax supported by the version that
builds it. The left column shows new syntax each version can assemble;
the right column shows new syntax first used in that version's source.

Ver New syntax supported             New syntax used in source
--- -------------------------------- ----------------------------
00  DATA $XX, ; comments             -
01  Single-character labels,         None
    DATA "string", DATA label
02  Non-standard mnemonics           Labels, label references,
    (LDA#, STAZ), whole-name         DATA "string"
    labels, $XXXX hex, \n escapes
03  None                             Non-standard mnemonics,
                                     whole-name labels
04  < > byte selectors,              Char escape literals
    label = $XX, * = $XXXX,
    new instrs (BITZ, BMI,
    BPL, SBCZ)
05  Two-pass (fwd refs),             = assignments, < > selectors,
    ~ branches, more instrs          * = origin
06  Hash tables (internal)           None
07  More instrs (via instgen),       None
    flag-based operand types
08  Error diagnostics, stderr,       ZP addressing without <
    line number tracking             (STAZ VAR not STAZ <VAR)
09  .include, file stack,            None
    more instructions
10  .zeropage, .code, ASLZ,         .include
    command-line arguments
11  Local labels (.prefix),          .zeropage, .code
    heap-based global labels
12  Standard 6502 syntax,            None (cannot self-host)
    all 13 addr modes, #'x',
    fwd ref tracking
13  None                             Standard 6502 syntax,
                                     #'x' character literals
14  Expressions (+, -), .data,       .data (replaces DATA)
    char lits as terms
15  .ifdef/.endif, define:           Expressions (+, -),
                                     char literal arithmetic
16  .macro/.endmacro, << >>,         .ifdef/.endif, define:
    optional label colons
17  .byte/.word/.asciiz/.reserve,    Colons, macros, << >>
    decimal, comma-separated
18  .ifndef, .else                   .byte, .word, .asciiz,
                                     decimal constants
